    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d341">

                <pb facs="0459" n="353" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg353"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-11-12"><hi rendition="#italic">November 12, 1890</hi>.</date>
                        (Received January 7, 1891.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1192.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose to you a
                    translation of the reply of the foreign office to my communication relating to
                    the Chinanfu troubles, a copy whereof was inclosed in my dispatch No. 1190, of
                    the 7th instant.</p>
                <p>It will be seen that the yamén reiterates the statement that I stated on divers
                    occasions that the missionaries did not insist on any particular tract of land.
                    Their action now, says the yamén, is at variance with former representations.
                    Nevertheless, the yamén has again addressed the governor of Shantung,
                    “requesting him to instruct the local authorities to satisfactorily discuss the
                    matter.” I await the answer of the governor to this suggestion.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby</hi>.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d341-a1.xml" xpointer="d341-a1"/>
            </div>
